            <ArticleTitle>Comparison of frequency of new coronary events in older subjects with and without valvular aortic sclerosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>599-600, A8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a prospective study of 1,980 subjects (mean age 81 +/- 8 years) without valvular aortic stenosis, 981 (50%) had valvular aortic sclerosis diagnosed by 2-dimensional and continuous-wave Doppler echocardiography. Independent risk factors for new coronary events were prior coronary artery disease (p = 0.0001, risk ratio 2.8), male gender (p = 0.002, risk ratio 1.3), and valvular aortic sclerosis (p = 0.0001, risk ratio 1.8).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
